source: crates/trousseau-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Re-encrypt the store, optionally changing how it is protected.

With no flags, re-encrypts to the same recipients (or passphrase) with a fresh file key. The entries
themselves do not change.

Usage: trousseau rekey [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --to-passphrase
          Convert to a passphrase store, or change the passphrase. Prompts twice

      --to-recipients <R>...
          Convert to a recipients store with exactly these recipients

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --store <PATH>
          Use this store file. Wins over `--global` and over store discovery
          
          [env: TROUSSEAU_STORE=]

      --global
          Use your personal store instead of the nearest project store (the `.trousseau` file in
          this directory or a parent)

      --identity <PATH>
          An identity (private key) file to try when unlocking. Repeatable. Also tried:
          `TROUSSEAU_IDENTITY_FILE`, the config file's `identity.files`, the default identity file,
          `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` and `~/.ssh/id_rsa`

      --passphrase-file <PATH>
          Read the store's passphrase from this file instead of prompting. One trailing newline is
          stripped

      --json
          Print one JSON document on stdout instead of text. Errors become a JSON object on stderr

      --quiet
          Suppress informational messages on stderr. Errors still print

      --no-input
          Never prompt. A command that would prompt fails instead: exit 4 for a secret, exit 2 for a
          confirmation

Examples:
  Re-encrypt with a fresh file key, same recipients or passphrase:
    trousseau rekey

  Change the passphrase of a passphrase store, or convert a recipients
  store to a passphrase store (prompts twice):
    trousseau rekey --to-passphrase

  Convert to a recipients store with exactly these recipients:
    trousseau rekey --to-recipients age1... "ssh-ed25519 AAAA... sam@laptop"

Notes:
  --to-recipients does not add you implicitly. Include your own recipient,
  or you will not be able to open the store afterward.
  To add or remove one recipient, 'trousseau recipients' is simpler.
